tilo for Debian
===============

The package installs the extension into the system extension directory but does
not enable it. Enabling an extension writes to the user's dconf, which a package
installed as root must not do, and which the user has not asked for. Enable it
from Settings, Extensions.

A copy in ~/.local/share/cinnamon/extensions/ takes priority over the one this
package installs, which is how a development checkout shadows the release.

 -- Jeffrey Gbeho <jeff.gbeho@gmail.com>
